{"name":"Chicory","hex":"#a78658","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chicory","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Either of two plants of the Asteraceae family.\n\n Common chicory (Cichorium intybus), source of Belgian endive, radicchio, and certain other cultivars with other names.","Common chicory (Cichorium intybus), source of Belgian endive, radicchio, and certain other cultivars with other names."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chicory"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chicory","blocks":[{"text":"Common chicory is a somewhat woody, perennial herbaceous plant of the family Asteraceae, usually with bright blue flowers, rarely white or pink. Native to Europe, North Africa, and western Asia, it has been introduced to the Americas, Australia, and South Africa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Illustration_Cichorium_intybus0_clean.jpg/330px-Illustration_Cichorium_intybus0_clean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicory","wikidata":"Q2544599"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Wegwarte_Cichorium_intybus.jpg/500px-Wegwarte_Cichorium_intybus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Wegwarte_Cichorium_intybus.jpg/500px-Wegwarte_Cichorium_intybus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWegwarte_Cichorium_intybus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Dried_chicory_root.jpg/500px-Dried_chicory_root.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Dried_chicory_root.jpg/1280px-Dried_chicory_root.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","sr